---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="ThemePark — AMOLED antireflective theme" description="One extension, one theme, total browsing antireflection.">
  <div class="hero">
    <div class="eyebrow">AMOLED antireflective theme</div>
    <h1>True black. True contrast. True matte.</h1>
    <p class="hero-tagline">
      ThemePark gives you one AMOLED antireflective theme that adapts to the light around you — dim in a dark room, bright in daylight, and pure white in sunlight for maximum contrast through the reflective veil.
    </p>
    <div class="cta-row">
      <a href="https://github.com/D1bakar/Theme-park/releases/latest/download/ThemePark-chrome.zip" class="btn btn-primary">
        <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
          <path d="M21 15v4a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2v-4"></path>
          <polyline points="7 10 12 15 17 10"></polyline>
          <line x1="12" y1="15" x2="12" y2="3"></line>
        </svg>
        Install ThemePark
      </a>
      <a href="https://github.com/D1bakar/Theme-park" class="btn btn-ghost">
        View on GitHub
      </a>
    </div>
    <p class="cta-note">
      Open source. No analytics. No accounts. All settings stay on your device.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="section-label">How it works</div>
  <div class="grid-2">
    <div class="card">
      <h3>AMOLED antireflective</h3>
      <p>
        True #000000 everywhere — buttons, cards, table cells, inline styles. No light surfaces survive.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Adaptive glare</h3>
      <p>
        Text luminance follows the light around you — dim at night, neutral indoors, bright in sunlight.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Per-site profiles</h3>
      <p>
        Fine-grained control over font size, line height, reading width, and animations — globally or per site.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Privacy-first</h3>
      <p>
        Zero network requests. No analytics. No accounts. All settings live in your browser.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div id="glare" class="section-label">Glare levels</div>
  <div class="grid-3">
    <div class="glare-card">
      <svg class="glare-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
        <path d="M21 12.79A9 9 0 1 1 11.21 3 7 7 0 0 0 21 12.79z"></path>
      </svg>
      <h3>Night</h3>
      <p>
        Dim text to avoid OLED halation in a dark room. Images dimmed hardest.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="glare-card">
      <svg class="glare-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
        <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="5"></circle>
        <path d="M12 1v2M12 21v2M4.2 4.2l1.4 1.4M18.4 18.4l1.4 1.4M1 12h2M21 12h2M4.2 19.8l1.4-1.4M18.4 5.6l1.4-1.4"></path>
      </svg>
      <h3>Indoor</h3>
      <p>
        Neutral tuning for ordinary indoor lighting. The default setting.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="glare-card">
      <svg class="glare-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
        <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="5"></circle>
        <path d="M12 1v2M12 21v2M4.2 4.2l1.4 1.4M18.4 18.4l1.4 1.4M1 12h2M21 12h2M4.2 19.8l1.4-1.4M18.4 5.6l1.4-1.4"></path>
        <path d="M12 17.5L12 23M8.5 12L3 12M15.5 12L21 12"></path>
      </svg>
      <h3>Sunlight</h3>
      <p>
        Pure white text for maximum contrast through the reflective veil. Links and hairlines brighten.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div id="install" class="section-label">Install</div>
  <div class="card">
    <ol class="steps">
      <li>
        <strong>Download the extension:</strong> <a href="https://github.com/D1bakar/Theme-park/releases/latest/download/ThemePark-chrome.zip">ThemePark-chrome.zip</a>
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Unzip the file</strong> to a folder on your computer.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Load it in Chrome or Brave:</strong> go to <code>chrome://extensions</code> or <code>brave://extensions</code>, enable "Developer mode", and click "Load unpacked".
      </li>
    </ol>
  </div>

  <div class="section-label">Known limits</div>
  <div class="card">
    <p>
      ThemePark is software-only: it maximizes legibility through external-light reflections, but it cannot remove physical reflections or apply a matte coating. Known limitations:
    </p>
    <ul style="color: var(--text-secondary); font-size: 14px; margin-left: 20px; margin-bottom: 0;">
      <li style="margin-bottom: 8px;">
        <strong>Photos via background-image</strong> — CSS has no selector for "element that has one", so photos painted this way stay full-bright. Gradient-only backgrounds are neutralised.
      </li>
      <li style="margin-bottom: 8px;">
        <strong>Closed shadow DOM</strong> — styles inside shadow trees are not reachable.
      </li>
      <li style="margin-bottom: 8px;">
        <strong>Video and canvas</strong> — these are rendered by the page, not by CSS.
      </li>
      <li style="margin-bottom: 8px;">
        <strong>Chrome:// pages, PDF viewer, and other restricted pages</strong> — these are out of scope for this extension.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</Base>
